select 'gases-solutions', 'Gas laws: Charles'' law', 'Charles'' law, or the law of volumes, was founded in 1787 by Jacques Charles. It states that, for a given mass of an ideal gas at constant pressure, the volume is directly proportional to its absolute temperature, assuming in a closed system. the volume (V) of a given mass of a gas, at constant pressure (P), is directly proportional to its temperature (T).', 'Wikipedia: Gas laws', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Gas_laws&oldid=1380424927', 'CC BY-SA 4.0. Wikipedia contributors (see page history). Excerpted and split into passages.'
